WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.332
Different chat checkpoints expect different special tokens and formatting around roles.

00:00:05.332 --> 00:00:13.522
The tokenizer's chat template converts a list of system, user, and assistant messages into the exact token sequence

00:00:13.522 --> 00:00:21.497
expected by that model. This is why a chat template should come from the checkpoint rather than being guessed manually.

00:00:21.497 --> 00:00:27.132
Two models can use the same visible messages but require different hidden formatting.

00:00:27.132 --> 00:00:30.810
The chat template handles that checkpoint-specific detail.
